Answer: The left-shift operator shifts the bits of a value toward the left. Example:

```java
int a = 2;
System.out.println(a << 1);
```

Output: 4 For positive integers, shifting left by one position multiplies the value by 2.

Answer: ```java
System.out.println(4 << 1);
System.out.println(4 << 2);
```

