Answer: The right-shift operator shifts the bits of a value toward the right. Example:

```java
int a = 8;
System.out.println(a >> 1);
```

Output: 4 For positive integers, shifting right by one position divides the value by 2.

Answer: ```java
System.out.println(16 >> 1);
